cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  T-XAI: A Threat-Model-Aware Contract for XAI Explanation Release
  in Cybersecurity — research artifact
message: >-
  The accompanying manuscript is under peer review and its authorship is withheld
  for that reason. Please cite this artifact anonymously; this file will be
  updated with author and publication metadata once review concludes.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-03'
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: Anonymous Author(s)
abstract: >-
  Measurement code and recorded results for a threat-model-aware explanation
  contract for XAI in cybersecurity. Computes the faithfulness, robustness and
  disclosure scores, the calibration condition, both sides of the theorem bridge
  between explanation robustness and action distributions, and the equilibrium of
  a Stackelberg release game, instantiated on public static-malware corpora. The
  governance layer of the contract — provenance, claim-evidence graph, and
  actionability — is specified in the manuscript but not exercised here, because
  the public corpora carry no telemetry provenance, analyst roles, or response
  playbook.
keywords:
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - cybersecurity
  - malware detection
  - adversarial machine learning
  - Stackelberg games
  - information disclosure
references:
  - type: data
    title: 'BODMAS: an open dataset for learning based temporal analysis of PE malware'
    url: 'https://whyisyoung.github.io/BODMAS/'
    notes: Primary corpus. Not redistributed with this artifact.
  - type: data
    title: 'EMBER: an open dataset for training static PE malware machine learning models'
    url: 'https://github.com/elastic/ember'
    notes: >-
      Second-corpus replication, and the source of the vendored feature
      extractor. Not redistributed with this artifact.
